[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:Food and Talk]
[00:01.62]Was Mrs. Rumbold a good companion at dinner? | 伦布尔德夫人是个好的晚餐伴侣吗？
[00:14.34]Last week at a dinner party, | 上周在一个晚宴上，
[00:17.42]the hostess asked me to sit next to Mrs. Rumbold. | 女主人请我坐在伦布尔德夫人旁边。
[00:22.23]Mrs. Rumbold was a large, | 伦布尔德夫人是个身材魁梧、
[00:24.97]unsmiling lady in a tight black dress. | 不苟言笑的女士，穿着一件紧身黑连衣裙。
[00:28.92]She did not even look up when I took my seat beside her. | 我在她身边坐下时，她甚至没有抬头看我。
[00:34.18]Her eyes were fixed on her plate and in a short time, | 她的眼睛盯着自己的盘子，不一会儿，
[00:39.02]she was busy eating. | 她就开始大吃起来。
[00:41.24]I tried to make conversation. | 我试图和她攀谈。
[00:44.52]'A new play is coming to "The Globe" soon,' | “一部新戏很快就要在‘环球剧场’上演了，”
[00:48.16]I said. 'Will you be seeing it?' | 我说，“您会去看吗？”
[00:52.56]'No,' she answered. | “不，”她答道。
[00:55.53]'Will you be spending your holidays abroad this year?' I asked. | “今年您会到国外度假吗？”我问。
[01:02.96]'No,' she answered. | “不，”她答道。
[01:05.47]'Will you be staying in England?' I asked. | “您会留在英格兰吗？”我问。
[01:09.64]'No,' she answered. | “不，”她答道。
[01:12.42]In despair, I asked her whether she was enjoying her dinner. | 绝望中，我问她是否喜欢她的晚餐。
[01:18.16]'Young man,' she answered, | “年轻人，”她回答说，
[01:21.39]'if you ate more and talked less, we would both enjoy our dinner!' | “如果你多吃点，少说点，我们俩都会享受晚餐的！”